Parts of nearest_neighbor/utils.py were borrowed upstream from Efficient-GPNN by Ariel Elnekave
(https://github.com/ariel415el/Efficient-GPNN); their notes are kept on the functions.

Modified for Autorig Workbench (2026):
- GenMM.py (the pyramid and match_and_blend), nearest_neighbor/losses.py (PatchCoherentLoss) and
  nearest_neighbor/utils.py (patch extraction and combination, distances, nearest neighbours) are ported from
  PyTorch and unfoldNd to NumPy, so they run on the CPU inside Blender's own Python with nothing installed.
- The CUDA device, tensorboard logging, progress bar and the upstream fork's keyframe pinning (it reads an
  undefined KEYFRAME_INDICES) are removed.
- The initial noise is Gaussian, scaled by each channel's spread and seeded; upstream adds unit noise times
  noise_sigma and wraps it with fmod(1).
- An example that loops also gives patches across its own seam.
- Motion data loading (BVH, Blender tracks) is not part of this port: autorig/core/motion_variants.py feeds it
  frames.
